[Module "module-1"]
[LessonId "m1-0001"]
[Title "King & Pawn vs King — Opposition"]
[Elo "800"]
[Theme "king and pawn, opposition"]
[Objective "Use the opposition to escort the pawn to promotion."]
[Intro "The most fundamental endgame: King and Pawn versus King. The key concept is the opposition — when two kings face each other with one square between them, the player who does NOT have to move holds the opposition and controls the critical squares."]
[FinalReflection "You held the opposition and promoted the pawn. This pattern decides thousands of games. Remember: the king must lead the pawn, not follow it."]
[MastersNote "The king must be in front of the pawn by at least one square to win."]
[SideToMove "white"]
[Mode "lecture"]

1. Ke6 {Advance the king in front of the pawn. This seizes the opposition.} Kd8 {Black steps aside.} 2. Kf7 {The key move! Step aside to control the promotion square and clear the path for the pawn.} Kd7 {Black tries to stay close to block.} 3. e6+ {The pawn advances with check.} Kd8 {Forced retreat.} 4. e7+ {The pawn safely marches forward.} Kd7 5. e8=Q+ {Promotion! The endgame principle is complete.} *

