[Module "module-1"]
[LessonId "m1-0002"]
[Title "Rook Endgame — Lucena Position"]
[Elo "900"]
[Theme "rook endgame, Lucena, bridge building"]
[Objective "Win using the bridge-building technique to promote the pawn."]
[Intro "The Lucena Position is the cornerstone of rook endgames. You have a pawn on the 7th rank with your king in front. The winning method is called 'building a bridge' — using your rook to shield the king from checks."]
[FinalReflection "You built the bridge perfectly. The Lucena Position appears in nearly every rook endgame — this technique alone is worth 100 rating points."]
[MastersNote "The bridge is built in four rook moves. Know this pattern cold."]
[SideToMove "white"]
[Mode "lecture"]

1. Rf4 {Step one of the bridge — bring the rook to the 4th rank to shelter the king.|The rook moves to prepare a shield.} Ra1 {Black waits, preparing to check the king from behind.} 2. Ke7 {The king steps out of the pawn's shadow.} Re1+ {Black begins checking.} 3. Kd6 {March the king toward the rook.} Rd1+ 4. Kc5 Rc1+ 5. Kd5 Rd1+ 6. Rd4 {The bridge is complete! The rook cuts off the black king's checks.} *

