[LessonId "m1-0003"]
[Title "Queen vs Rook — Philidor's Method"]
[Elo "1000"]
[Theme "queen vs rook, Philidor, technique"]
[Objective "Winning queen vs rook requires a specific technique to avoid stalemate."]
[Intro "Queen versus rook is a theoretical win, but it requires precise technique. The main danger is stalemate. The easiest way to win is to force the defending king away from its rook, setting up a fork or a skewer."]
[FinalReflection "Excellent technique. Forcing the King away from the Rook using a skewer is the most direct way to resolve this endgame."]
[MastersNote "Never rush. Stalemate traps are everywhere."]
[SideToMove "white"]
[Mode "puzzle"]

1. Qa5+ {The queen delivers a skewer along the fifth rank.|Check!} Kc4 {The king must step away, leaving the rook defenseless.|Forced move.} 2. Qxh5 {White wins the rook and the game.|The skewer is complete.} *

