[Module "module-1"]
[LessonId "m1-0004"]
[Title "Rook vs Pawn — Philidor's Draw"]
[Elo "850"]
[Theme "rook endgame, Philidor, drawing technique"]
[Objective "Hold the draw with a rook against a passed pawn using the Philidor method."]
[Intro "When you have a rook and your opponent has a passed pawn about to promote, the drawing technique is to place your rook on the 6th rank (the Philidor position). This cuts off the enemy king until the pawn advances, at which point you drop the rook behind for perpetual checks."]
[FinalReflection "You held the Philidor draw. This technique saves countless endgames. The key idea: rook on the 6th holds, rook behind the pawn draws if timed correctly."]
[MastersNote "Rook on the 6th rank — not the 7th, not the 5th. The 6th."]
[SideToMove "white"]
[Mode "lecture"]

1. d6 {The pawn reaches the 6th rank.|White pushes the pawn.} Ra1! {The key to the Philidor! Once the pawn advances, drop the rook behind to check.|The rook drops to the back rank.} 2. Ke6 {White's King steps up to threaten mate or promote.|The king advances.} Re1+ {Check from behind! The White king has nowhere to hide.|Start checking from behind.} 3. Kd5 {King steps back.} Rd1+ {Keep checking.} 4. Ke5 {King moves again.} Re1+ {Perpetual check!|The Philidor repetition holds the draw.} *